# Python is exec'd, not just read.
#
# tools/tui-pty-drive.py runs under WSL on Windows and is invoked through its
# shebang. A CRLF checkout turns line 1 into `#!/usr/bin/env python3\r`, and
# Linux then reports:
#
#   env: 'python3\r': No such file or directory
#
# Which reads exactly like a missing interpreter and cost a full debugging
# session chasing the wrong thing - the pty suite failing three times while the
# TypeScript under test was demonstrably fine. Pinning LF means a Windows
# checkout cannot produce a Python file that cannot be run.
*.py text eol=lf

# Shell scripts, same reason: a CRLF shebang is a `not found` on any POSIX host.
*.sh text eol=lf
